# Clang configuration for the conda target triple.
#
# <CFGDIR> expands to the directory holding this file, so every path here
# follows the prefix wherever it is installed - no environment variable, no
# activation script, no relocation step.
#
# The name is not decorative. Clang looks for `<triple>-<driver>.cfg` where the
# triple is its own DEFAULT TARGET, which our build sets via LLVM_HOST_TRIPLE
# to @TRIPLE@ on this platform. So a plain `clang` invocation finds this file
# with no symlink involved.
-isystem <CFGDIR>/../include
$-Wl,-L,<CFGDIR>/../lib
$-Wl,-rpath,<CFGDIR>/../lib
$-Wl,-rpath-link,<CFGDIR>/../lib
--sysroot=<CFGDIR>/../@TRIPLE@/sysroot
